    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f688a40b_0aaaa824",
        "filename": "board/c2d2/board.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 241,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002022
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-01-09T09:09:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "in the clk hack below I mess around with the MODER pins.  I realize now that this could be used to avoid the endpoint crash when not in SPI mode.\nSimply always have the SPI block enabled, but set the GPIO MODER to be inputs.\nWhen this function gets called, instead of configuring the module from scratch, just update the MODER as appropriate (keeping in mind the CLK hack below).\nProbably still want to do some of the block reset stuff below, though, just for sanity\u0027s sake.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 241,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 241,
        "endChar": 19
      },
      "revId": "0bcd439250680ede621fb0c5da73714b1a1d36f2",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f65145df_700c598a",
        "filename": "board/c2d2/board.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 265,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002022
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-01-09T09:09:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "this is actually quite sloppy, and causes a significant glitch (extra rising edge of clk) between here and the next line.\n\nit would be better instead to do the equivalent of \"spi_enable 0\" here, which could be as simple as resetting the SPI block and swinging MODER.\n\nafaikt this gets called when the SPI endpoint gets closed (i.e., flashrom quits)",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 265,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 265,
        "endChar": 41
      },
      "revId": "0bcd439250680ede621fb0c5da73714b1a1d36f2",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
