      },
      "lineNbr": 279,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002022
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-01-09T09:13:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "actually, the larger stm32f072s have 3 possible pins for each SPI*_CLK.\n\nSo a generic implementation should probably just have the configuration include a gpio_clk field.  Setting this field could also be the indicator for whether to do this drive optimization trickery or not, if selectable at runtime.",
      "parentUuid": "4a6cc943_83c2b986",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 279,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 279,
        "endChar": 49
      },
      "revId": "0bcd439250680ede621fb0c5da73714b1a1d36f2",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5b3f1024_d6702ebd",
        "filename": "chip/stm32/spi_master.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 280,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002022
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-01-09T09:09:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "no need to optimize this.  the key detail is that the mode is switched after all bits have been sent but *before* we disable the digital SPI block (clearing SPE)",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 280,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 280,
        "endChar": 48
      },
      "revId": "0bcd439250680ede621fb0c5da73714b1a1d36f2",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9cbfe829_3c497d11",
        "filename": "chip/stm32/spi_master.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 397,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002022
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-01-09T09:09:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I moved this in the hope of minimizing the window for glitches, but at this point I\u0027m pretty certain it\u0027s not necessary to do so.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 397,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 397,
        "endChar": 40
      },
      "revId": "0bcd439250680ede621fb0c5da73714b1a1d36f2",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c09c75aa_92c59021",
        "filename": "chip/stm32/spi_master.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 405,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002022
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-01-09T09:09:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "originally I tried pre-calculating cr1 so that it could be set immediately after MODER, avoiding a race entirely.\nIt resulted in about 200ns of floating, which was enough of a glitch to trigger the level shifter\u0027s one-shot high-pulse when there\u0027s less capacitive loading.  With a real Hatch board, the floating was not sufficient to trigger the one-shot (and write+verification worked), but it was a large enough spike to cause concern.\n\nThe concern with this implementation is if there\u0027s any delay between enabling the SPI block and setting the pin alternate mode, clocks could be lost and the whole transaction will be bit-shifted.  Maybe disabling interrupts before and after is sufficient; it\u0027s just two register assignments.\n\nWith this ordering, the waveform looks perfect.  It\u0027s not clipping the first rising edge at all.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 405,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 405,
        "endChar": 28
      },
      "revId": "0bcd439250680ede621fb0c5da73714b1a1d36f2",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ef5cbff9_e7dd24a5",
        "filename": "chip/stm32/spi_master.c",
